# 🔷 2. How to Save Cost in GCP (Especially GKE)

Cost optimization is HUGE in real-world systems.

---

## 💸 Top Cost-Saving Strategies

### ✅ 1. Use Autopilot or Right Node Sizing

Over-provisioning = wasted money
Use:

  GKE Autopilot OR
  Right-sized node pools

---

### ✅ 2. Enable Cluster Autoscaler

Automatically adds/removes nodes:

bash
gcloud container clusters update my-cluster \
  --enable-autoscaling \
  --min-nodes=1 \
  --max-nodes=5


👉 Saves money during low traffic

---

### ✅ 3. Use Spot/Preemptible VMs

Up to 80% cheaper
Good for:

  Batch jobs
  Non-critical workloads

---

### ✅ 4. Set Resource Requests/Limits

Bad example ❌:

yaml
resources:
  requests:
    cpu: "2"


Good example ✅:

yaml
resources:
  requests:
    cpu: "200m"


👉 Prevents over-allocation

---

### ✅ 5. Scale Pods Automatically (HPA)

yaml
apiVersion: autoscaling/v2
kind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler
spec:
  minReplicas: 1
  maxReplicas: 5


---

### ✅ 6. Turn Off Idle Resources

Delete unused:

  Load balancers
  Persistent disks
  Old clusters

---

### ✅ 7. Use Committed Use Discounts

If workload is stable → reserve capacity → cheaper

---

### ✅ 8. Use Cloud Storage Lifecycle Rules

Auto-delete old backups/logs

---

## 🧠 Golden Rule

👉 “Don’t pay for idle resources”

