# 🔷 3. How to Fix Restarting Pods (CrashLoopBackOff)

This is one of the most common Kubernetes issues.

---

## 🔍 Step-by-Step Debugging

### ✅ Step 1: Check Pod Status

bash
kubectl get pods


Look for:


CrashLoopBackOff
Error
OOMKilled


---

### ✅ Step 2: Check Logs

bash
kubectl logs <pod-name>


For previous crash:

bash
kubectl logs <pod-name> --previous


---

### ✅ Step 3: Describe Pod

bash
kubectl describe pod <pod-name>


Look for:

Events
Errors
Health check failures

---

## 🚨 Common Causes & Fixes

---

### ❌ 1. Application Crash

Cause:

Bug in code

Fix:

Check logs
Fix exception

---

### ❌ 2. Wrong Environment Variables

yaml
env:
  - name: DB_HOST
    value: wrong-host


👉 Fix config

---

### ❌ 3. Port Mismatch

App runs on 8080 but container expects 80

---

### ❌ 4. Liveness Probe Failure

K8s kills pod repeatedly

Fix:

yaml
livenessProbe:
  initialDelaySeconds: 30


---

### ❌ 5. Out Of Memory (OOMKilled)

bash
Reason: OOMKilled


Fix:

yaml
resources:
  limits:
    memory: "512Mi"


---

### ❌ 6. Dependency Not Ready

App starts before DB is ready

Fix:

Use readiness probe
Add retry logic

---

## 🧠 Debug Tip

Always follow:

👉 Logs → Describe → Events → Fix

