# 🔷 4. Difference: Liveness vs Readiness Probe

This is very important in interviews and production.

---

## 🔍 Liveness Probe

👉 Checks: *“Is the app alive?”*

If FAIL → Kubernetes restarts the container

---

## 🔍 Readiness Probe

👉 Checks: *“Is the app ready to serve traffic?”*

If FAIL → Pod is removed from service (no traffic)
NOT restarted

---

## 📊 Comparison

| Feature  | Liveness        | Readiness        |
| -------- | --------------- | ---------------- |
| Purpose  | Detect crash    | Detect readiness |
| Action   | Restart pod     | Stop traffic     |
| Use case | Deadlock, crash | DB not ready     |

---

## 📦 Example

yaml
livenessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /health
    port: 8080
  initialDelaySeconds: 30
  periodSeconds: 10

readinessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /ready
    port: 8080
  initialDelaySeconds: 5
  periodSeconds: 5


---

## 🎯 Real-World Example

### Scenario:

App depends on DB

App starts → DB not ready yet

### What happens?

✅ Liveness → OK (app running)
❌ Readiness → FAIL → no traffic

👉 Prevents user errors

---

## 🧠 Simple Analogy

Liveness = “Are you alive?”
Readiness = “Can you work?”

---

